{
  "_comment": [
    "How this index has been revised. One row per change to an app's monthlyCost in",
    "src/data/apps.json, reconstructed from git history on 2026-09-05 and committed",
    "here so it stops depending on git.",
    "",
    "WHY COMMITTED RATHER THAN DERIVED",
    "astro.config.mjs already shells out to `git log` for sitemap lastmod, so a",
    "git-derived log would have had precedent. It would also break on a shallow CI",
    "clone, and this record will outlive the reason it was created. It is data now.",
    "APPEND BY HAND when a price moves. Do not rewrite history in it.",
    "",
    "WHAT `kind` MEANS — this is the honest part, and the page states it too:",
    "  corrected  our figure was wrong; a sourced figure replaced it",
    "  withdrawn  we had published a figure the vendor does not actually publish;",
    "             the claim was withdrawn rather than replaced",
    "  narrowed   the figure was right but open-ended (\"$39+\"); reading the vendor",
    "             page fixed it to an exact entry price on a named plan",
    "  added      a new app entered the index",
    "  changed    THE VENDOR moved its price between two of our observations",
    "",
    "As of 2026-09-05 not one row is `changed`. Every entry is us revising our own",
    "record against a source. That makes this an audit trail, not a price history,",
    "and it must never be labelled as the latter. The vendor-change series starts",
    "at the first row that earns `kind: \"changed\"`."
  ],
